{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fifth popular-stretchy-mussel plan-repair batch — 2026-09-05\n\nAudited and repaired the four remaining named unaudited leaves against the immutable code basis `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. The isolated audit worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/comment-remediation-3e32` was clean and still at that exact commit; the moving `origin/main` ref was not substituted for the frozen basis.\n\nThe AST/token census considered all 1,114 true leading-docstring or maximal full-line-comment blocks across 72 owned modules and selected exactly 185 bloated blocks (139 docstrings, 46 comment regions; 15,746 before-words):\n\n- `general-brinish-kookaburra` (`0933-ced1-b660-43d7`): 18 paths; 43 blocks (25 docstrings, 18 comment regions; 3,425 words). Split mixed old ranges into stable owners/anchors, including the recovery output-cap/step-ID regions and workflow sidecar/DET pairs; preserved input-rejection/outage, raw fail-closed propagation, insufficiency disposition, concurrency, Pass-1 warm/usage, hierarchy, telemetry, redispatch, output-floor, and archive cleanup/redaction contracts.\n- `moleskin-literal-stagbeetle` (`0d4e-673c-6039-48cb`): 18 paths; 54 blocks (35 docstrings, 19 comment regions; 4,560 words). Remapped shifted attribution/editor spans, split the completion and editor regions by stable scope, and explicitly protected the concise `_NINE_FD4_CHARS` motivating-size comment. Preserved observed model/usage/provenance, graph scope, outage disposition, pinned prefetch, physical/economic bounds, no-elision, typed recovery, PASS-cache concurrency, child certification, DET, and editor-policy contracts.\n- `scrawny-ingenious-civet` (`1129-21f3-be2f-40fa`): 18 paths; 32 blocks (31 docstrings, 1 comment region; 3,069 words). Corrected the two stale autodeploy numeric spans, which now contain executable code, to the unchanged sequenced-`df` comment and measurement docstring. Preserved portable API, DSSE/SSHSIG/op-cert, gate-ref, ticket-root, audit rendering, authorship forensics, capped-prune, and exempt-minus-bug-tier contracts.\n- `femoral-armed-mantis` (`1ed7-4540-91b1-4645`): 18 paths; 56 blocks (48 docstrings, 8 comment regions; 4,692 words). Replaced “long plumbing/history docstrings” and “dense bug-history sections throughout” with a complete stable allowlist; protected the concise provenance defect oracles, the wiring JSON round-trip comment, and Anthropic-key setup note. Preserved pricing, run-shape, DC-doc, uv, provider/gateway/Bedrock provenance, verifier, Verified-parity, identity, op-cert, wall-clock, web-tool, WIP, and workflow-name contracts.\n\nEvery description is below the 8,000-character admission cap (7,084 / 7,823 / 6,041 / 7,747 characters respectively). Each defines path-qualified `D:<qualified-owner>` and `C:<innermost-scope>:before:<unchanged-code-anchor>` IDs; immutable-before/final `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; removal only of allowlisted leading docstrings; normalization only of `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; equality of all remaining ASTs; and token rejection of changed inline or non-allowlisted comments. Runtime strings, regexes, prompts, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing lines are protected. Each also requires exactly one non-author TSV PASS row per block with full immutable/final citations, word counts, preserved contract/consumer, `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n\nConsumer searches covered imports, source/path guards, workflow selectors, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, and pydoc. Material consumers recorded in the plans include the plan-review fixture import, dynamic redispatch loader, authorship fixture-maintenance reader, audit-server source spy, audit-page import-convention pair, API generator/docs, ADR 0059 provenance citations, wall-clock exclusion script, and verifier/web contract siblings. No runtime docstring consumer reads an allowlisted value.\n\nImmediately before mutation, MCP readback confirmed all four leaves were `open`, `assignee=null`, and `attestations={}`. Applied exactly three MCP mutations per leaf (12 total): `edit_ticket(description)`, `set_file_impact`, and `set_verify_commands`. Every result was `ok`, every `push_status.state` was `ok`, and every description/cross-session warning was null.\n\nStrict MCP readback then matched all four descriptions byte-for-byte, all 72 ordered path/reason rows exactly, and all 20 normalized DD command triples exactly. Each leaf records exactly five commands: focused pytest including real consumers, scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path diff integrity, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`. All four remain open, unassigned, and unsigned.\n\nNo source/test file was edited. No leaf was claimed or transitioned; no plan review, completion verifier, test suite, implementation gate, commit, manual push, or close was run. The only mutations were normal rebar ticket events, auto-committed and auto-pushed by the MCP server."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788629507621137265,"uuid":"15896259-ccaa-4043-a436-f25be5aa4ea7"}